      "candidateRole": "You are the gastroenterology dietitian.",
      "patientRole": "A 48-year-old delivery driver with chronic pancreatitis who stopped drinking alcohol a year ago. Two months ago his consultant started pancreatic enzyme capsules for pale, oily, floating stools that are hard to flush, and weight loss. He has come because his symptoms are no better. He has been taking the capsules after his evening meal only.",
      "patientConcern": "Because toilets are hard to find on his rounds, he has cut almost all fat out of his diet and skips lunch at work. He believes this is the sensible thing to do.",
